menu "OpenShock LED drivers"

    config OPENSHOCK_RGB_LED_DITHERING
        bool "Temporal dithering on the RGB LED"
        default y
        help
            The WS2812B takes 8 bits per channel. With dithering the driver keeps 16 bits per
            channel (color times brightness) and alternates between the two nearest 8-bit
            steps from frame to frame, so the average shows the 16-bit value: smooth colors
            and fine dimming at low brightness, where 8 bits are coarsest. Frames only go out
            while a channel sits between two steps.

            Off, each color is rounded to the nearest 8-bit step and sent once.

    config OPENSHOCK_RGB_LED_DITHER_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Dither frame interval (ms)"
        depends on OPENSHOCK_RGB_LED_DITHERING
        range 1 10
        default 1
        help
            Time between dithered frames. Shorter keeps the alternation above what the eye
            sees; the slowest fractions (1/256 of a step) still take 256 frames to come
            around. Each frame costs an RMT transmission of about 30 us.

endmenu
